// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// EstateOS — Prisma schema
// Derived from realestate-crm-ux-spec.md v1.0, §22 (data model) and the status
// machines in §6.4, §7.6, §8.5, §9, §10, §11, §12, §14.
//
// Design decisions applied (confirmed before generation):
//
//  1. Money is BigInt paise everywhere. Never Float, never Float. Serialize to
//     string at the API boundary — JSON cannot carry BigInt.
//  2. Multi-tenancy: aggregate roots carry a real `company` relation. Child rows
//     that inherit scope through a parent carry an indexed `companyId` scalar
//     only, so Company does not accumulate 65 back-relations. Every query must
//     still filter on companyId (§25).
//  3. createdById / updatedById are scalar ids, not relations, to keep User from
//     growing ~40 back-relation arrays. Domain-meaningful actors (owner,
//     assignee, approver, holder) are proper relations.
//  4. Two invariants from §22 need PARTIAL unique indexes, which Prisma cannot
//     express. They live in prisma/migrations/00000000000000_partial_indexes.
//     Without that migration both invariants are unenforced at the DB level.
//  5. Soft delete everywhere (deletedAt). Note this weakens every unique
//     constraint — see the partial-index migration for unit_code and lead phone.
//  6. Activity is polymorphic (entityType + entityId, no FK) so one timeline
//     spans leads, bookings, units and customers. No referential integrity there.
//  7. PAN / Aadhaar / bank fields are String holding CIPHERTEXT. Prisma has no
//     encryption layer; encrypt and decrypt in the application (§25).
//
// Additions beyond the §22 entity list, required by rules stated elsewhere in
// the spec: UnitStatusHistory (§7.6), ReceiptAllocation (§11.4 allocation is
// many-to-many), ProjectMember (§6.2 step 6).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "mongodb"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

